    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/sa-iv-art-gallery-and-studio-assistant-iwgi-visual-art-faculty-of-arts/": {
      "title": "SA IV – Art Gallery and Studio Assistant – IWGI Visual Art, Faculty of Arts",
      "description": "SA IV – Art Gallery and Studio Assistant – IWGI Visual Art, Faculty of Arts | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities SA IV – Art Gallery and Studio Assistant – IWGI … SA IV – Art Gallery and Studio Assistant – IWGI Visual Art, Faculty of Arts Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 8, 2026 Classification : Student Assistant IV Employee Group : PSAC Job Title : Art Gallery and Studio Assistant Department : IWGI Visual Art, Faculty of Arts Wage or Salary : $21.63/hour Number of Hours to Work : up to 10 hours/week Start Date : Sept.15, 2026 Number of Positions available : 2 End Date of Employment : April 30, 2027 Course title and number (if applicable) : NA Date Issued: Sept.1, 2026 Qualifications/Experience : Preference will be given to graduate students or Brandon University third-fourth year undergraduate students. The successful candidate must have a background in contemporary visual art and experience in art handling in a gallery or museum setting. Applicants who lack either a background in the visual arts or museum studies will not be considered for the position. Applicants should be familiar with the production and distribution of online promotional material (PSA, press releases, email list-serves). Experience with website updating and maintenance an asset. Work experience in a recognized art gallery or museum is preferred. Experience hanging and handling art is necessary. The successful candidate will have good interpersonal and creative problem-solving skills and work well under pressure. The candidate should be flexible regarding work hours. Key Duties : Working with the Gallery and Studio Coordinator to fulfill duties such as: Preparation – Mounting and removal of art installations in the Sutherland Gallery/ Umphrey Building space, General art studio assistance and Maintenance Online promotion of gallery events via social media, email advertising, website updates, email press release distribution Office and research – outreach to highschools to develop programming and engage the public, photocopying and other office related duties and other relevant duties as assigned. To Apply: Please send a cover letter and resume (CV) with two references to vaachair@brandonu.ca Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
