    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/athletics-and-recreation-assistant/": {
      "title": "Athletics and Recreation Assistant",
      "description": "Athletics and Recreation Assistant | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Athletics and Recreation Assistant Athletics and Recreation Assistant Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 7, 2026. Classification: Student Assistant III Job Title: Athletics & Recreation Assistant Department: Athletics & Recreation Wage or Salary: $18.41/hr Hours of Work: 8-12 hours per week Start Date: September 11, 2026 Number of Positions available: 1 Length of Appointment: 09/11/2026 to 08/31/2027 Date Issued: August 31 , 2026 Duties: Assist with inventory management of athletic equipment, canteen and merchandise, and organization of storage rooms Assist with Campus Recreation events, organizing and communicating with Campus Recreation teams Update and disseminate athletic game night signage, such as menus and VIP areas Monitoring of sports equipment and reporting on wear or shrinkage Ability to relate to visitors of a varied age and of diverse populations Other related duties as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: Preference given to Brandon University students Ability to work independently with minimal supervision and/or with others effectively Considerable advance skills and judgment with attention to detail Experience with sport event management would be an asset Interest and knowledge of sports (specifically basketball, volleyball and soccer) is an asset To apply please send a resume to: Russ Paddock, Director of Athletics & Recreation paddockr@brandonu.ca Brandon University Bobcats Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons