    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/student-assistant-iv-school-of-music-6/": {
      "title": "Student Assistant IV – Orchestra Studio Assistant – School of Music",
      "description": "Student Assistant IV – Orchestra Studio Assistant – School of Music | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Student Assistant IV – Orchestra Studio Assistant &#82… Student Assistant IV – Orchestra Studio Assistant – School of Music Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 9, 2026 Classification: Student Assistant IV Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Studio Assistant (Orchestra) Department: Music Wage: $21.63 per hour Hours of Work: 5 hours per week Start Date: September 10, 2026 Number of Positions Available: 1 Length of Appointment: April 11, 2027 Date Issued: September 2, 2024 Duties: Assist the faculty member with: – Maintain regular contact with instructor; – Assist with organizing of studio materials and arranging repertoire; – Assist with research related to delivery of studio instruction; – Assist with coaching and assessment of techniques as required; – Assist students with performance practice, skill-building, technique development, and equipment in-between lessons; – Other relevant duties as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: 1. Considerable advanced skills and judgement. 2. Ability to work independently and/or with others effectively. 3. Ability to communicate clearly. 4. Strong attention to detail, excellent problem solving skills, and self-motivated. 5. Basic math skills. Education: 1. Preference given to current Brandon University Music student; with enrolment in graduate program or holding a graduate degree. 2. Specific courses related to the given department/faculty in which the job in needed when indicated in the posting. 3. Strong academic standing. To Apply: Please forward resume outlining your experience by email to: Bobbi White, School of Music, Brandon University at: white@brandonu.ca. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/student-assistant-iv-school-of-music-3/": {
      "title": "Student Assistant IV- Level IV Marker – School of Music",
      "description": "Student Assistant IV- Level IV Marker – School of Music | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Student Assistant IV- Level IV Marker – School of Musi… Student Assistant IV- Level IV Marker – School of Music Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 8. 2026 Classification: Student Assistant IV Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Level IV Marker Department: Music Wage: $21.63 per hour Hours of Work: 5-7 hours per week Start Date: September 9, 2026 Number of Positions Available: Up to 8 Length of Appointment: April 30, 2027 Date Issued: September 1, 2026 Various Duties: -Maintain contact with supervising professor weekly. -Grade a variety of class assignments specific to the position and course, which can include the following: sight-signing, dictation, part-writing, analysis, counterpoint, short compositions, writing assignments (short paragraphs, reading responses, short essays). -Grade the final exam. -Report on frequent problems encountered in assignments, and on possible plagiarism. -Organize time efficiently in order to finish assignments within a short turn-around window. -Other related duties as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: -School of Music graduate student preferred; upper-year undergraduates accepted. -Knowledge of core music theory, history, and/or aural skills is essential. -Previous experience with courses and their textbooks is preferred. -Good English communication skills. -Detail-oriented. -Comfortable working independently and making independent judgments. -Basic math skills. -Familiarity with online platforms such as Zoom, Moodle and Microsoft Teams is required. To Apply: Please forward a resume outlining your experience by email to Bobbi White, School of Music, Brandon, University at: white@brandonu.ca. When applying, please indicate if you wish to have your name remain on an eligibility list for the 2026-27 academic year. Brandon University is committed to equity, welcomes diversity, and hires on the basis of merit. All qualified individuals who may contribute to the diversification of the University, especially women, persons with disabilities, Indigenous persons, racialized persons, and persons of all sexual orientations and genders are encouraged to apply. Canadian citizens and permanent residents are given priority. Evidence of citizenship must be provided. We are committed to providing an inclusive and barrier-free work environment. This starts with the hiring process. If you require an accommodation during any phase of the evaluation process, please advise HR at hr@brandonu.ca. All information received related to an accommodation is kept confidential. To ensure this employment opportunity is accessible to all interested individuals, this posting is available in an alternate format upon request. Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities – Open Positions Application Form                         (not required for Faculty positions) Contact Us Human Resources Room 337, Clark Hall 270 - 18th Street Brandon, Manitoba R7A 6A9 Phone: (204) 727-9782 Fax: (204) 726-1957 Email: hr@brandonu.ca © 2014–2026 Brandon University Contact Us Emergency Info Accessibility Log in"
    },
    "https://www.brandonu.ca/jobs/job/student-assistant-ii-department-of-physics-astronomy-21/": {
      "title": "Student Assistant II – Department of Physics & Astronomy",
      "description": "Student Assistant II – Department of Physics & Astronomy | Employment Opportunities Top Toolbar Links Webmail Campus Map Contact Us Brandon University Search Site: Primary Navigation Future Students Programs Current Students Athletics Alumni Services Brandon University Employment Opportunities Student Assistant II – Department of Physics & Ast… Student Assistant II – Department of Physics & Astronomy Applications are to be received by: 4:30 p.m. on September 7, 2026 or until filled Classification: Student Assistant II Employee Group: PSAC Job Title: Assignment Marker/Lab Marker Department: Physics & Astronomy Wage: $17.63 per hour Hours of Work: see table below Start Date: September 14, 2026 Number of Positions Available: 2 Length of Appointment: until December 14, 2026 Course title and number: 74.151 General Physics I Date Issued: August 31, 2026 Duties: The Department of Physics and Astronomy invites applications for Student Assistants for the following courses during the Fall 2026 term: 74:151 General Physics I    Assign. Marker    Up to 6 hrs per wk for up to 9 wks 74:151 General Physics I    Lab Marker          Up to 6 hrs per wk for up to 10 wks The successful candidates will mark assignments or lab reports from a marking key, and other related duties as assigned. Qualifications/Experience: • Successful completion of course(s) for which they are applying • Demonstrated success in other Physics courses • Ability to meet deadlines (reliable and punctual) • Ability to interpret and follow marking guide • Ability to use judgement to evaluate alternative solutions To Apply: Apply in writing with a cover letter that shows clearly for which position(s) you would like to be considered, your experience, and how you meet the above qualifications. Please submit your application with any supporting documentation to: Dr. Todd Fugleberg, Associate Professor and Chair, Department of Physics and Astronomy, Brandon University; 270 – 18th Street; Brandon, 